WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.268
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:04.170
You're here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.638
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:08.508
I want to wish everyone
a very happy Thanksgiving.

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:10.042
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.042 --> 00:00:12.845
Happy Thanksgiving!
Happy Thanksgiving.

00:00:12.845 --> 00:00:14.781
Happy Thanksgiving.

00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:17.316
I didn't miss celebrating
over Zoom,

00:00:17.316 --> 00:00:18.785
but I definitely missed
that mute button.

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.586
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.586 --> 00:00:22.355
Yeah, the holiday
is pretty much over,

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:25.124
which means right now everyone's
back with their immediate family

00:00:25.124 --> 00:00:26.659
talking smack about
everyone else.

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:28.128
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.128 --> 00:00:30.429
On Thanksgiving, there are
always two kinds of families --

00:00:30.429 --> 00:00:32.564
the one that wakes up early
to run a 5K

00:00:32.564 --> 00:00:34.367
and the one that stays up late
to reheat all the food

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:36.669
they just put away. It's like,
"Alright, who's hungry?

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:38.738
Let's make some sandwiches.
Come on!"

00:00:40.806 --> 00:00:42.608
I read that more than half
of all people

00:00:42.608 --> 00:00:44.344
said that they were
exercising in the weeks

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:46.879
leading up to Thanksgiving.

00:00:46.879 --> 00:00:48.213
You know, it might be time
to cut back

00:00:48.213 --> 00:00:50.049
when we're all training
for a meal, don't you feel?

00:00:50.049 --> 00:00:51.684
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:53.352
Yeah, the first Thanksgiving
was celebrated

00:00:53.352 --> 00:00:55.922
400 years ago in 1621.

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:59.692
That's right.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:01.460
That was the first time
someone finished eating,

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:02.595
then looked at their spouse
like,

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:04.497
"When are they gonna leave?"

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:06.599
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:08.201
But I hope everyone had
a nice Thanksgiving.

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:10.136
It was a fun day of trying
to figure out...

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:12.205
[ Cheers and applause ]
I hope you had fun.

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:16.776
Yeah, it was a fun day of
trying to figure out

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:18.177
if Uncle Ralph's vaccinated

00:01:18.177 --> 00:01:20.213
without actually asking
if he's vaccinated.

00:01:20.213 --> 00:01:21.547
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.547 --> 00:01:22.582
How are you doing, Uncle Ralph?

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:23.983
Is that a Band-Aid
on your shoulder?

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:26.252
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.154
Second shot hurt worse
than the first one?

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:30.556
[ Laughter ]
Third one?

00:01:30.556 --> 00:01:31.624
That's right, people took

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:33.860
vaccination status
very seriously,

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:35.294
though I thought it was weird
to see a bouncer

00:01:35.294 --> 00:01:36.763
outside Grandma's House.

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:38.498
I.D. and vax card.

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:39.699
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:42.101
You can go see Nona.

00:01:42.101 --> 00:01:45.304
Of course, a lot of people like
to drink wine on Thanksgiving.

00:01:45.304 --> 00:01:48.874
I love how --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:48.874 --> 00:01:50.910
I love how my aunt puts away
three glasses and said,

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.645
"Boy, that turkey
really makes you sleepy."

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:56.249
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:59.051
Yep, 63% of people drink wine,

00:01:59.051 --> 00:02:02.621
19% drink beer,
and 10% drink liquor,

00:02:02.621 --> 00:02:04.456
while the other 8%
mix all that together

00:02:04.456 --> 00:02:07.527
and wake up on Christmas.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:09.128
They're here
in the audience tonight.

00:02:09.128 --> 00:02:13.999
[ Cheers and applause ]
Welcome.

00:02:13.999 --> 00:02:16.001
And in the band. Wow.

00:02:16.001 --> 00:02:17.837
This year, as always,

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:21.841
the food people feared to cook
the most was the turkey.

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.276
If you take it out too late,
it's dry.

00:02:23.276 --> 00:02:24.543
If you take it out too early,

00:02:24.543 --> 00:02:26.045
you got to rub it down
with Purell.

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:27.713
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.713 --> 00:02:29.015
Turkeys are always
scary to cook,

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:30.716
especially if you deep-fry it.

00:02:30.716 --> 00:02:32.885
The only thing more dangerous
than your dad saying,

00:02:32.885 --> 00:02:34.953
"I'm going to go deep-fry
the turkey" is him saying,

00:02:34.953 --> 00:02:37.056
"I'm going to go knock
the icicles off the gutters."

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:39.125
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:40.927
Whoa! Oh, my God!

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:45.297
Actually, I read
the tofu turkeys went up

00:02:45.297 --> 00:02:47.800
in sales this year.
It's a little different.

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:49.969
Instead of people saying
white or dark meat,

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:51.971
they go, "Gray
or slightly grayer meat?"

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:54.307
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:55.875
Meanwhile, I read that
most Americans prefer

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:58.778
Thanksgiving leftovers
to the actual dinner.

00:02:58.778 --> 00:03:02.014
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:02.014 --> 00:03:04.150
When asked why, they say,
"'Cause I get to eat it alone

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:06.685
over the sink."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.685 --> 00:03:09.755
That's the best. Come on.

00:03:09.755 --> 00:03:12.591
I read that air travel this week
was expected to nearly reach

00:03:12.591 --> 00:03:14.527
pre-pandemic levels

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:16.395
to accommodate
all of the extra passengers.

00:03:16.395 --> 00:03:18.163
Delta and American
added flights,

00:03:18.163 --> 00:03:20.900
while Spirit added another row
of folding chairs to the wings.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:22.702
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.075 --> 00:03:30.576
That's right, a lot of people
were traveling

00:03:30.576 --> 00:03:32.278
for the first time
in over a year.

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:33.613
So things were
a little hectic.

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:35.781
Here, check out this news story
I saw about it.

00:03:35.781 --> 00:03:38.951
-Many are traveling
for the first time since 2019.

00:03:38.951 --> 00:03:41.888
So expect to deal with all sorts
of people at the airport,

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:44.056
including the person
in the TSA line

00:03:44.056 --> 00:03:46.693
who has apparently never taken
their shoes off in their life,

00:03:46.693 --> 00:03:48.928
the people in Zone 17
who stand in the way

00:03:48.928 --> 00:03:50.829
while everyone else
is boarding,

00:03:50.829 --> 00:03:52.831 line:0%
the person chugging a gallon
of Aquafina

00:03:52.831 --> 00:03:55.301 line:0%
because they didn't realize
it counted as a liquid,

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:57.236
people who don't have
their boarding pass handy,

00:03:57.236 --> 00:03:59.072
even though they just spent
half an hour in line

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:00.974
being told to have it handy,

00:04:00.974 --> 00:04:04.443
and, of course, the hardest
thing to deal with -- babies.

00:04:04.443 --> 00:04:06.379
-That's right.
Yeah, interesting.

